{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551431-pokemon-trainer-what-caste","id":1551431,"title":"Pokemon trainer, what caste?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-02T14:56:40-07:00","id":1551431,"title":"Pokemon trainer, what caste?","content":"So if a Pokemon trainer came into Creation and Exalted on the basis of their skill as a Pokemon battler, which caste of each Exalted type would be best (for types with unusually Exaltation requires, like Sidereals or Getimian, just we say they are destined/resurrected/etc)?<br /> How I see it:<br /> <br /> Solars: Dawn (combat) or Zenith (leadership)<br /> <br /> Lunars: Changing moon or New moon (cunning and intelligence vs the forceful approach of Full moons)<br /> <br /> Dragon Blooded: Wood aspect (taming animals)<br /> <br /> Sidereals: Battles, maybe Serenity occasionally (Battles being any sort of fighting while Serenity would for entertainment side).<br /> <br /> Abyssal: Dusk and Midnight (same reasons as solars)<br /> <br /> Alchemicals: Orichalcum or Starmetal (glorius leader vs cunning strategist)<br /> <br /> Getimian: Vernals, maybe? (Show offs, not too sure with them).<br /> <br /> Infernal: Azimuth or Ascendant (Same reasons as Solars).<br /> <br /> Liminal: No idea.<br /> <br /> Exigent: Chosen of gladiators or Pokemon battles.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-02T16:36:16-07:00","id":1551432,"title":"","content":"For Solars, Zenith is a good pick, but so are Twilight and Eclipse. Twilights get Medicine as a Caste Ability, allowing you to quickly heal your mons, and Eclipses MIGHT be able to learn Pokemon Moves. Emphasis on MIGHT. In comparison, a Dawn would be more of a fighter by themselves rather than actually using their Pokemon to fight.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised that you didn't mention Chosen of Journeys at all. Having Ride as a Caste Ability really helps for catching Pokemon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-03T01:56:15-07:00","id":1551437,"title":"","content":"How the Full Moons do Pokemon: &quot;I choose myself.&quot; (Turns into elephant. It's super effective!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-04T14:35:03-07:00","id":1551465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/foru